  "description": "KEBVAQ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H81 Dy4 N24 O17 3+,3(Cl1 O4 1-),2(C2 H3 N1),C1 H4 O1,4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.536-5.067 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.90-178.57°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C109H99Cl3Dy4N26O34. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
